"2052","Abdullah ibn Ja'far reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ seated me behind him on his mount one day and whispered to me a hadith that I shall not narrate to anyone. The most beloved thing for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to screen himself with for his needs was a target or a grove of palm trees. He entered a garden belonging to a man of the Ansar, and there was a camel. When it saw the Prophet ﷺ, it groaned and its eyes shed tears. The Prophet ﷺ came to it and wiped its forehead and its hump, so it became calm. He said: ""Who is the master of this camel? To whom does this camel belong?"" A young man of the Ansar came and said: ""It is mine, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""Do you not fear Allah concerning this beast which Allah has given you possession of? For it has complained to me that you starve it and overwork it."""
"2053",""
