"2058",""
"2059","Ziyad ibn Jubayr ibn Hayyah narrated: My father informed me that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Al-Hurmuzan: ""Since you have been spared, then advise me."" This was because he had said to him: ""Speak, there is no harm,"" so he granted him safety. Al-Hurmuzan said: ""Yes, Persia today is a head and two wings."" He asked: ""Where is the head?"" He said: ""Nahavand, with Bendar."" He said: ""Then with him are the Asawira of Kisra and the people of Isfahan."" He asked: ""Where are the two wings?"" Al-Hurmuzan mentioned a place which I have forgotten. Al-Hurmuzan said: ""Cut off the two wings and you will weaken the head."" Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: ""You lie, O enemy of Allah! Rather, I will aim for the head, and Allah will cut it off; and when Allah cuts it off from me, the two wings will be cut off from me."" Then Umar intended to march to it himself. They said: ""We remind you of Allah, O Commander of the Faithful, that you march yourself to the Persians (Al-Ajam); for if you are killed, there will be no order for the Muslims. But send the armies."" He said: So he sent the people of Madinah, and he sent among them Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he sent the Muhajirun and the Ansar. And he wrote to Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari: ""March with the people of Basrah."" And he wrote to Hudhayfah ibn Al-Yaman: ""March with the people of Kufah, until you all gather at Nahavand together. When you have gathered, your commander is An-Nu'man ibn Muqrin Al-Muzani.""فَلَمَا اجْتَمَعُوا بنهاوند أَرْسَل إِلَيْهِم بُنْدَار (العلج) أَن أَرْسِلُوا إِلَيْنَا يَا مَعْشَر الْعَرَب رَجُلًا مِنْكُم نُكَلِّمُهُ، فَاخْتَار النَّاسُ الْمُغِيَرة بن شعبة، قال أَبِيْ: فَكَأَنِّي أَنْظُرُ إِلَيْه رَجُلٌ طويلٌ، أَشْعَثَ أعورَ، فَأَتَاهُ، فَلَمَّا رَجَعَ إِلَيْنَا سَأَلْنَاهُ؟ فَقَال لَنا: إِنِّي وَجَدْتُ الْعَلَج قَد اسْتَشَار أَصْحَابه في أَيِّ شَيْءٍ تَأْذَنُون لِهَذَا العربي؟ أَبَشَارَتُنَا وَبَهْجَتُنَا وَمُلْكُنَا؟ أَوْ نَتَقَشَّفُ لَهُ، فَنَزْهَدُهُ عَمَّا في أَيْدِيَنَا؟ فَقَالُوا: بَل نَأْذَن لَه بِأَفْضَل ما يَكُون من الشَّارَة والعدة، فَلَمَّا رَأَيْتُهُم رَأَيْتُ تِلْكَ الحِرَاب، وَالدَّرَق يَلْمَعُ مِنْهُ البَصَر، وَرَأَيْتُهُم قِيَامًا عَلَى رأسه، وَإِذَا هُو عَلَى سَرِيرٍ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ، وَعَلَى رَأْسِهِ التَّاجُ، فَمَضَيْتُ كَمَا أَنَا، وَنَكَسْتُ رَأْسِي لِأَقْعُد مَعَه عَلَى السرير، قال: فَدُفِعْتُ وَنُهِرْتُ، فَقُلْتُ إِن الرُّسُل لَا يُفْعَلُ بِهْم هَذا، فَقَالُوا لِي : إِنَّمَا أَنْتَ كَلْبٌ أَتَقْعُد مَعَ الْمَلِكِ؟!، فَقُلْت: لَأَنَا أَشْرَفُ في قَوْمِي مِنْ هَذَا فِيْكُمْ، قَالَ : فَانْتَهَرَنِي، وَقَالَ: اِجْلِسْ، فَجَلَسْتُ، فَتُرْجِمَ لِي قَولُه؟ فَقَال: يَا مَعْشَرَ الْعَرَبِ! إِنَّكُم كُنْتُم أَطْوَل النَّاس جُوْعًا، وَأَعْظَم النَّاس شَقَاءً، وَأَقْذَرَ النَّاس قَذَرًا، وَأَبْعَد النَّاس دارًا، وأَبْعَدَهُ مِنْ كُلِّ خَيْرٍ، وَمَا كَان مَنَعَنِي أَن آمُر هَذِه الأَسَاوِرَةِ حَوْلِي، أَنْ يَنْتَظِمُوْكُمْ بِالنِّشَابِ، إِلَا تَنْجِيْسًا لِجِيَفِكُمْ لِأَنَّكُم أَرْجَاسٌ، فَإِن تَذْهَبُوا يُخَلّٰي عَنْكُمْ، وَإِنْ تَأْبُوا نُبَوِّئُكُمْ مَصَارِعَكُمْ،""Translation: When they gathered at Nahavand, Bendar (the Alaj - a derogatory term for a non-Arab/Persian noble) sent to them saying: ""Send to us, O company of Arabs, a man from among you that we may speak to him."" The people chose Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. My father said: ""It is as if I see him now, a tall man, disheveled, one-eyed. He went to him. When he returned to us, we asked him. He said to us: 'I found the Alaj had consulted his companions: ""In what do you permit this Arab? Is it in our good tidings, our joy, and our kingdom? Or do we endure hardship for him, so that he may renounce what is in our hands?"" They said: ""Rather, we permit him with the best possible insignia and equipment."" When I saw them, I saw those spears and shields, dazzling the sight. I saw them standing at his head, and there he was on a bed of gold, and on his head was the crown. I walked on as I was, and lowered my head to sit with him on the bed. He said: I was pushed and rebuked. I said: ""Messengers are not treated like this."" They said to me: ""You are but a dog; do you sit with the King?!"" I said: ""I am more noble among my people than this one is among you."" He rebuked me and said: ""Sit."" So I sat. His speech was translated for me. He said: ""O company of Arabs! You were the most hungry of people, the most wretched of people, the filthiest of people, the farthest of people from home, and the farthest from all good. Nothing prevented me from ordering these Asawira around me to pepper you with arrows, except the defilement of your corpses, for you are impure. If you leave, we will leave you alone; and if you refuse, we will assign you your places of slaughter.""'""قال الْمُغِيَرة : فَحَمَدْتُ الله وَأَثْنَيْتُ عَلَيْهِ، وَقُلْتُ : وَالله ما أَخْطَأَتَ مِنْ صِفَتِنَا وَنَعْتِنَا شَيْئًا، إِنْ كُنَّا لَأَبْعَد النَّاس دَارًا وَأَشَدّ النَّاس جُوعًا وَأَعْظَم النَّاس شَقَاءً وَأَبْعَد النَّاس من كُل خَيْرٍ حَتَّى بَعَثَ الله إِلَيْنَا رَسُوْلًا، فَوَعَدَنَا بِالنَّصْر في الدُّنْيَا وَالْجَنَّة في الآخرة، فَلَم نَزَلْ نَتَعَرَّفُ مِنْ رَبِّنَا مُذْ جَاءَنَا رَسُولُه صلی اللہ علیہ وآلہ وسلم الفَلاح، وَالنَّصْرَ، حَتَّى أَتَيْنَاكُمْ، وَإِنَّا وَالله نَرَى لَكُم مُلْكًا وَعَيْشًا لَا نَرْجِعُ إِلَى ذَلِكَ الشَّقَاءِ أَبَدًا، حَتَّى نَغْلِبَكُمْ عَلَى مَا فِي أَيْدِيْكُمْ، أَو نُقْتُلَ في أَرْضِكُمْ، فَقَال : أَمَّا الأعور، فَقَد صَدَقَكُم الَّذِي في نفسه، فَقُمْتُ مِنْ عِنْدِهِ، وَقَد وَالله أرْعَبْتُ الْعَلْج جهدي، فَأَرْسَل إِلَيْنَا الْعَلْج إِمَّا أَن تَعْبُرُوا إِلَيْنَا بِنَهَاوَنْد، وَإِمَّا أَنْ نَعْبُرَ إِلَيْكُمْ، فَقَال النُّعْمَان : اُعْبُرُوا، فَعَبَرْنَا قَالَ أَبِي : فَلَم أَر كَالْيَوْم قَطُ، إِن الْعُلُوج يجيئون، كَأَنَّهُم جِبَال الحَدِيْد، وَقَدْ تَوَاثَقُوا أَنْ لَا يَفِرُّوا مِنَ العَرَبِ، وَقَد قُرن بَعْضُهُم إِلَى بَعْضٍ، حَتَّى كَان سَبْعَةٌ في قران، وَأَلْقَوْا حَسَك الْحَدِيد خَلْفَهُمْ، وَقَالُوا : من فَر مِنَّا عقره حَسَك الحديد، فَقَال الْمُغِيَرة بن شُعُبَة حِين رَأَى كَثْرَتَهُم : لَم"""
"2060",""
"2061","From Humayd (meaning: Ibn Hilal) who said: There was a man from Al-Tufawah whose route passed by us. He came to the tribe and narrated to them, saying: ""I arrived in Medina with a caravan of ours and we sold our merchandise (the original manuscript reads 'our sale'). Then I said: 'I will surely go to this man so that I may bring back news of him to those after me.' He said: So I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found him showing me a house. He said: 'A woman used to live in it (meaning a house in Medina). She went out in a military expedition of the Muslims and left behind twelve she-goats of hers, and her spindle with which she used to spin. He said: Then she lost a she-goat from her flock and her spindle. She said: ""O Lord, You have guaranteed for whoever goes out in Your path that You will protect his property, and I have lost a she-goat from my flock and my spindle, and I beseech You for my she-goat and my spindle."" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began mentioning the intensity of her beseeching her Lord, Blessed and Exalted. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Then her she-goat was found in the morning, and another like it, and her spindle, and another like it, and those (the original twelve). So go to her and ask her if you wish.'"""
"2062","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""The first of people against whom judgment will be pronounced on the Day of Resurrection will be a man who died a martyr. He will be brought forth and Allah will make known to him His favors and he will recognize them. He will say: 'What did you do about them?' He will say: 'I fought for You until I died a martyr.' He will say: 'You have lied, but you fought that it might be said: ""He is courageous."" And so it was said.' Then he will be ordered to be dragged along on his face until he is cast into Hellfire.And [another will be] a man who acquired knowledge and taught it and recited the Qur'an. He will be brought forth and Allah will make known to him His favors and he will recognize them. He will say: 'What did you do about them?' He will say: 'I acquired knowledge and taught it and recited the Qur'an for Your sake.' He will say: 'You have lied, but you acquired knowledge that it might be said: ""He is a scholar,"" and you recited the Qur'an that it might be said: ""He is a reciter."" And so it was said.' Then he will be ordered to be dragged along on his face until he is cast into Hellfire.And [another will be] a man whom Allah made rich and gave him all kinds of wealth. He will be brought forth and Allah will make known to him His favors and he will recognize them. He will say: 'What did you do about them?' He will say: 'I left no path in which You like money to be spent without spending in it for Your sake.' He will say: 'You have lied, but you did it that it might be said: ""He is generous."" And so it was said.' Then he will be ordered to be dragged along on his face until he is cast into Hellfire."""
"2063","Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), said: ""When Makkah became constricted for us, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) were harmed and tested, and they saw the affliction and trial befalling them in their religion, and that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) could not ward that off from them — while the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was in a position of protection from his people and his uncle, nothing of what he disliked reaching him from what befell his companions — the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to them: 'Indeed, in the land of Abyssinia there is a king under whom no one is wronged, so go to his land until Allah makes for you a way out and relief from what you are in.' So we went out to it in groups until we gathered there, and we settled in the best of abodes with the best of neighbors; we were secure in our religion and did not fear any injustice from him."""
"2064",""
"2065",""
"2066",""
"2067",""
"2068","Buraydah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on one of his military expeditions. When he returned, a black slave girl came and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I vowed that if Allah returned you safely, I would beat the duff before you and sing."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: ""If you vowed, then beat it; otherwise, do not."" So she began to beat it. Then Abu Bakr entered while she was beating it, then ʿAlī entered while she was beating it, then ʿUthmān entered while she was beating it, then ʿUmar entered and she threw the duff beneath her buttocks and sat upon it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Indeed, Satan fears you, O ʿUmar. I was sitting while she was beating it; then Abu Bakr entered while she was beating it, then ʿAlī entered while she was beating it, then ʿUthmān entered while she was beating it, but when you entered, O ʿUmar, she threw the duff."""
"2069",""
"2070",""
"2071",""
"2072","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Allah the Almighty has undertaken for the one who goes out in His cause, not being driven out except for jihad in My cause and belief in Me and affirmation of My messengers, that he is guaranteed by Me that I will admit him to Paradise or return him to his dwelling from which he went out, having obtained what he attained of reward or spoils. And by Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad! There is no wound received in the cause of Allah except that it will come on the Day of Resurrection in the same condition as when it was received; its color the color of blood, and its scent the scent of musk. And by Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad! Were it not that it would be difficult for the Muslims, I would never have stayed behind from any expedition fighting in the cause of Allah. But I do not find the means to carry them, and they do not find the means to follow me, and it would be hard on their souls to stay behind after me. And by Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad! I would love to fight in the cause of Allah and be killed, then fight and be killed, then fight and be killed."
"2073",""
"2074",""
"2075",""
"2076",""
"2077",""
"2078",""
"2079",""
"2080","From Abu Taybah: Shurahbil ibn al-Mustat called for Amr ibn Abasah al-Sulami and said: ""O Ibn Abasah! Will you narrate to me a hadith that you heard yourself from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, in which there is no addition, no lie, and you do not narrate it from someone else who heard it other than you?"" He said: ""Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say:'Any man who shoots an arrow in the cause of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and it reaches its target, whether missing or hitting, for him is a reward equal to that of freeing a slave from the descendants of Ismail.And any man who grays a hair in the cause of Allah, it will be a light for him.And any Muslim man who frees a Muslim man, every limb of the freed person will ransom a limb of the freer from the Fire.And any Muslim woman who frees a Muslim woman, every limb of the freed woman will ransom a limb of the freer from the Fire.And any Muslim man who presents to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, from his own loins three children who did not reach the age of puberty, or a woman [who does the same], they will be a shield for him from the Fire.And any man who rises for ablution intending prayer, and perfects the ablution in its proper places, he will be secure from every sin or offense he has committed. Then if he stands for prayer, Allah will raise him by it a degree; and if he sits, he sits secure.'"""
"2081",""
"2082",""
"2083",""
"2084",""
"2085","On the authority of Abu al-Darda', from the Prophet ﷺ who said: ""There are three whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves; He laughs to them and rejoices over them: The one who, when a detachment is exposed, fights behind it with his life for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, so either he is killed, or Allah grants him victory and suffices him; then Allah says: 'Look at My servant, how he patiently offered his life for Me.' And the one who has a beautiful wife and a soft, comfortable bed, then he rises from the night — leaving his desire — so he remembers Me and converses intimately with Me, though if he wished he could have slept. And the one who is on a journey and has a company with him, so they stay up late and exert themselves, then they sleep, so he stands at the pre-dawn time in ease or hardship."""
"2086",""
"2087",""
"2088",""
"2089",""
"2090",""
"2091",""
"2092",""
"2093","Talq ibn Habib al-Basri narrated that Abu Taliq told them: His wife, Umm Taliq, came to him and said: ""The Hajj season has arrived, O Abu Taliq."" He had a camel and a she-camel; he would perform Hajj on the she-camel and go on military expeditions on the camel. She asked him to give her the camel to perform Hajj on it. He said: ""Do you not know that I have dedicated it for the cause of Allah?"" She said: ""Indeed, Hajj is of the cause of Allah, so give it to me, may Allah have mercy on you."" He said: ""I do not wish to give it to you."" She said: ""Then give me your she-camel and you perform Hajj on the camel."" He said: ""I will not prefer you with it over myself."" She said: ""Then give me from your provisions."" He said: ""I have nothing surplus beyond my needs and my family's needs to take with me or leave for you."" She said: ""Indeed, if you gave it to me, Allah would replace it for you."" He said: ""When I refused her, she said: 'When you come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, convey my greetings of peace to him and inform him of what I said to you.'"" He said: ""So I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, conveyed her greetings of peace to him, and informed him of what Umm Taliq had said."" He said: ""Umm Taliq spoke the truth. If you had given her the camel, it would have been in the cause of Allah; if you had given her your she-camel, it would have been in the cause of Allah, and you would have been in the cause of Allah; if you had given her from your provisions, Allah would have replaced it for you."" He said: ""And she asks you, O Messenger of Allah, what equals Hajj (with you)?"" He said: ""An Umrah in Ramadan."""
