"2102",""
"2103",""
"2104","Aslam Abu Imran said: We went on an expedition from Medina intending Constantinople (and over the people of Egypt was Uqbah ibn Amir), and over the army was Abdur-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Al-Walid. The Romans had their backs pressed against the city wall. Then a man from among us charged at the enemy, and the people said: ""Hold on, hold on! There is no god but Allah, he is throwing himself into destruction with his own hands."" Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari said: ""You interpret this verse only thus: 'If a man charges to fight seeking martyrdom or to prove himself,' but this verse was revealed concerning us, the Ansar, when Allah supported His Prophet and made Islam manifest. We said secretly among ourselves, away from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him): 'Come, let us stay with our wealth and improve it.' So Allah the Exalted revealed: 'And spend in the way of Allah and do not throw yourselves with your own hands into destruction.' So throwing yourselves with your own hands into destruction means that we stay with our wealth and improve it and abandon jihad."" Abu Imran said: Abu Ayyub did not cease to strive in the way of Allah until he was buried in Constantinople."
