"2126","On the authority of Ya'la ibn Munyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) announced a military expedition, and I was an old man with no servant. So I sought a hired man to assist me, on the condition that I would give him his share of the spoils. I found a man, and when the departure drew near, he came to me and said: ""I do not know what the shares are, nor what my share will amount to; guarantee me something, whether there is a share or not."" So I stipulated three dinars for him. When the spoils were present, I intended to give him his share, but I remembered the dinars. So I went to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and informed him of the matter. He said: ""I find nothing for him in this expedition of his, in this world or the Hereafter, except the dinars he stipulated."""
"2127",""
"2128",""
"2129",""
"2130","(2130) Habib ibn Shihab al-Anbari said: I heard my father say: I came to Ibn Abbas, I and a companion of mine, and we met Abu Hurayrah at the door of Ibn Abbas. He said: ""Who are you two?"" We informed him, and he said: ""Go to a people who have dates and water; each valley flows only according to its capacity."" We said: ""Much good is in you; seek permission for us to see Ibn Abbas."" So he sought permission for us, and we heard Ibn Abbas narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) delivered a sermon on the day of Tabuk and said: ""There is no one among the people like a man holding the reins of his horse, striving in the cause of Allah and avoiding the evils of people. And like a Bedouin man among his sheep, who hosts his guest and fulfills his right."" I said: ""Did he say that?"" He said: ""He said it."" I said: ""Did he say that?"" He said: ""He said it."" I said: ""Did he say that?"" He said: ""He said it."" So I magnified Allah, praised Allah, and thanked Him."
"2131",""
"2132","On the authority of Jarwal Zuhayr ibn Surad al-Jushami, who said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took us captive on the day of Hunayn—the day of Hawazin—and proceeded to distribute the young men and captives, I recited this poetry to him:""Bestow your favor upon us, O Messenger of Allah, in generosity,For you are the man we hope for and await.Bestow favor upon a people whom fate has afflicted,Their unity scattered, their fortunes changed by time.Time has left them crying out in grief,Upon their hearts are gloom and overwhelming sorrow.If your bounty does not reach them, spreading its grace,O most forbearing of people when tested.Bestow favor upon women who once nursed you,When your every action and inaction adorned you.Do not make them like one whose honor has been stripped away,So preserve us, for we are a noble people.We indeed give thanks for blessings when they are denied,And we have stored up [good deeds] after this day.So clothe with pardon those whom you once nursed,From your mothers, for pardon is well-known.O best of those whom noble steeds pranced beneath,At the onset of battle when sparks of war ignite.We hope for a pardon from you that we may wear,O guide of creation, when you pardon and prevail.So pardon, and may Allah pardon what you dread,On the Day of Resurrection when victory is granted to you.""When he heard this poetry, he said: ""What was mine and belongs to the Banu Abd al-Muttalib is yours."" Quraysh said: ""What was ours is for Allah and His Messenger."" And the Ansar said: ""What was ours is for Allah and His Messenger."""
