"2166","On the authority of Umm Salamah: That Zaynab, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), when the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) emigrated, sought permission from her husband Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi' to go to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), so he gave her permission and she came to him. Then Abu al-As caught up with her in Medina and sent word to her saying: ""Seek protection for me from your father."" So she went out and poked her head out from the door of her chamber while the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was leading the people in the morning prayer. She said: ""O people! I am Zaynab bint Muhammad, and I have granted protection to Abu al-As."" When the Prophet (peace be upon him) finished the prayer, he said: ""O people! I did not know about this until I heard it from you. Verily, the protection granted by the lowest of the Muslims is binding upon all Muslims."""
